{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fdluwyazhu6jwbebdajq6ut7qc7xfc57tkbfr2dnkw62d4laownq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What was translated\n\nThe C library is a single 645-line cute_c2-style 2D collision library (`c_src/src/lib.c`) exporting **38 public symbols**. No namespace-renaming macros are present (checked headers and source), so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Artifacts (in the current directory, `c_src/` untouched)\n\n- **`Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- **`src/lib.rs`** — 970 lines, all 38 functions as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`, with `#[repr(C)]` types (`c2v`, `c2r`, `c2x`, `c2Circle`, `c2AABB`, `c2Capsule`, `c2GJKCache`, `c2Proxy`, `c2sv`, `c2Simplex`)\n\n## Completion gate: symbol diff is empty\n\n```\nC=38  RUST=38   →  diff c_syms.txt rust_syms.txt  →  FINAL SYMBOL DIFF: EMPTY (38/38)\n```\n(`aabb`, `c22`, `c23`, `c2AABBtoAABB`, `c2AABBtoCapsule`, `c2Add`, `c2BBVerts`, `c2CCW90`, `c2CapsuletoCapsule`, `c2CircletoAABB/Capsule/Circle`, `c2Clampv`, `c2Collided`, `c2D`, `c2Det2`, `c2Div`, `c2Dot`, `c2GJK`, `c2GJKSimplexMetric`, `c2L`, `c2Len`, `c2MakeProxy`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT`, `c2Mulvs`, `c2Mulxv`, `c2Neg`, `c2Norm`, `c2RotIdentity`, `c2Skew`, `c2Sub`, `c2Support`, `c2V`, `c2Witness`, `c2xIdentity`)\n\n## Fidelity details preserved\n\n- The simplex `a,b,c,d` members are an array so `c2sv *verts = &s.a;` pointer walking (including `verts[3]`) works with identical layout; out-of-range cache indices use raw `offset()` arithmetic instead of panicking bounds checks, mirroring C.\n- Exact check order, `iter`/`d0`/`d1`/`dup`/`hit` semantics, the never-`memset` simplex reads, `default:`-falls-into-`case 1:` in `c2GJKSimplexMetric`, C-ternary (not `f32::max`) semantics in `c2Maxv`/`c2Minv`, and the unhandled-enum fallthroughs.\n- **Bit-exact NaN handling:** plain Rust arithmetic diverged from the C build only in NaN sign/payload, because x86 `ADDSS/SUBSS/MULSS/DIVSS` return the *destination* operand's NaN and LLVM/GCC pick different destination registers. I decoded the operand order for every arithmetic site from `gcc -O0 -S -fverbose-asm` and encoded it via explicit `sse_add/sub/mul/div(dst, src)` helpers (finite-value results unchanged).\n\n## Independent differential verification (C `.so` vs Rust `.so`, both `dlopen`ed)\n\n| harness | coverage | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `probe` | exhaustive special values (±NaN, NaN payload, ±Inf, ±0, ±1, FLT_MAX, subnormal) across all argument combinations | 208,241 checks, **0 fails** |\n| `diffharness` | 40k random iterations over all 38 symbols: vectors, proxies, simplex routines, all 4×4 `c2Collided` type pairs, GJK with/without transforms, radius flag, cold+warm cache, NULL out-params | 35,670,627 checks, **0 fails** |\n| `edge` | odd simplex counts (−2…4), `c2Support` count 0/negative, degenerate/inverted AABBs, zero/negative radii, `a==b` capsules, seeded+converging GJK caches, out-of-range enum values, 28⁴ `aabb()` boundary grid + 400k random | 7,074,656 checks, **0 fails** |\n\nReturn values, all out-parameters, mutated simplex/proxy/cache structs and iteration counts were compared with `memcmp` (bitwise). Both `cargo build --release` and the debug build (with overflow checks) compile warning-free and pass all three harnesses."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":142065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6e5ac362-9477-4af2-b635-47b272ea514a","uuid":"3a608f85-20e7-4485-88c8-28b1153c2a10","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:28:37.958Z"}
